### Exponential backoff with jitter

Source: https://github.com/taskforcesh/bullmq/blob/master/docs/gitbook/guide/retrying-failing-jobs.md

Adds a jitter option to the exponential backoff strategy, generating random delays between the calculated exponential delay and that delay multiplied by jitter (e.g., between 192000 ms and 96000 ms for delay 3000 and jitter 0.5 on the 7th attempt).

```typescript
import { Queue } from 'bullmq';

const myQueue = new Queue('foo');

await queue.add(
  'test-retry',
  { foo: 'bar' },
  {
    attempts: 8,
    backoff: {
      type: 'exponential',
      delay: 3000,
      jitter: 0.5,
    },
  },
);
```

